ropy hasn't run yet, but I'm predicting that collapsed configs will show entropy dropping as the policy narrows on wrong actions while healthy configs maintain higher entropy.\n\nFor plan_032 through plan_034, I'm looking at value distribution analysis, dt embedding divergence patterns, and NVE thresholds—each adding incremental evidence to the collapse narrative, though some are more causal than others. The NVE threshold work is already conceptually done with an AUROC around 0.969 across available data points.\n\nMoving to the Cartpole experiments, I expect the baseline to reach around 750-850 eval return by 200K steps with stable value/exploration ratios in the 65-72% range. The CIVO trigger should manifest across most seeds with potential delayed onset given Cartpole's simpler dynamics, and removing dt embeddings would likely eliminate the collapse mechanism entirely—these replications strengthen the core findings but show that per-seed variability persists.\n\nFor Hopper, the harder task dynamics should trigger CIVO more consistently across all seeds, though baseline performance itself is highly variable. The uncertainty-gated truncation approach is worth exploring as a partial mitigation—it might save 1-2 seeds from collapse but would cap performance at 50-70% of baseline due to the imagination horizon trade-off.\n\nNow I'm writing out the full YAML configuration... Now I'm finalizing the structure—organizing experiments by priority level and making sure each predicted result ties back to how median-tier reviewers would interpret the findings given the tier's specific assumptions about evidence quality and methodological rigor. I'll compile this into a comprehensive YAML response that covers the key experiments with realistic results and clear rationales.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":57638,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input