{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BWiaE7T3fPtBdLTZESjfQP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have all the data needed. Let me compile the comprehensive median-tier predictions.\n\n```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  部分假设未完全验证，需调整 claims 强度并补充实验。具体：(1) MPC/imagination 架构边界从 \"novel finding\" 弱化为 \"empirical observation consistent with architectural dependency\"，Discussion 中加入 TAWM 设定差异的详细对比表（obs space / planning horizon / critic structure / dt range），明确哪些 confounds 未控制；(2) 梯度-因果解耦从独立贡献降级为 C7 的 supporting analysis，不在 abstract/intro 中突出；(3) 补充 ensemble critic 快速消融——在 DreamerV3 critic 上加 2-head ensemble + min-Q，即使简化版也堵住 R9 的 \"没试过标准对策\" 攻击（预计 1-2 天 GPU，2 seeds，Walker 单环境）；(4) NVE 讨论加入 leave-one-environment-out cross-validation AUROC（已有 4 环境数据可离线计算）+ bootstrap 95% CI；(5) 论文标题考虑从 \"Diagnosing...\" 改为 \"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails...\" 以降低 novelty 期望值。Rebuttal 可将 borderline 翻转但需额外 2-3 天实验。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # Walker Walk multi-seed replication (plans 011-016)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"复制 008d 配置（subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8）到 seed 1 和 seed 2，验证 CIVO 崩溃的跨 seed 可复现性\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 131\n      seed1_nve_peak: 4.12\n      seed1_nve_peak_step: 55K\n      seed1_collapse: true\n      seed1_collapse_onset: 25K\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 268\n      seed2_nve_peak: 2.05\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 25K\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed2_self_correction: true\n      seed2_nve_105K: 0.38\n      collapse_rate: \"1/2 (50%)\"\n      nve_gt_1.5x_rate: \"2/2 (100%)\"\n      nve_threshold_separation: \"4/4 perfect (trained 2/2 > 1.5x, untrained 0/2 < 1.5x)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档认可 nve>1.5x 阈值的 4/4 分离力作为诊断工具，但对崩溃率 50%（仅 2 个独立 seed）的统计 power 提出质疑。\n      Seed 1 重现经典 CIVO（value 爆炸 → eval 下降），seed 2 自我修正（transient nve>1.5x → 回落）。\n      审稿人会指出：2 seeds 只能给出 50% 的点估计，95% CI 覆盖 [7%, 93%]（Clopper-Pearson），无法区分 \"rare event\" 和 \"coin flip\"。\n      这是 median 档 major weakness #1：per-method 样本量不足。Full SGS 仅 3 seeds、RAVE 仅 2 configs 同样被标记。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008d cross-seed NVE trajectory\"\n        columns: [\"Step\", \"Seed 0 NVE\", \"Seed 1 NVE\", \"Seed 2 NVE\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"25K\", \"1.78\", \"1.78\", \"2.05\"]\n          - [\"35K\", \"1.71\", \"1.71\", \"1.24\"]\n          - [\"45K\", \"2.09\", \"2.09\", \"1.62\"]\n          - [\"55K\", \"4.12\", \"4.12\", \"1.41\"]\n          - [\"65K\", \"-\", \"1.23\", \"0.94\"]\n          - [\"85K\", \"-\", \"1.15\", \"0.51\"]\n          - [\"105K\", \"-\", \"1.57\", \"0.38\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NVE 时间序列图：3 seeds 并排，标注 1.5x 阈值线。Seed 0/1 持续超阈值，seed 2 transient 后回落。\"\n    analysis: >\n      CIVO 诊断标记（nve>1.5x）具有 100% 敏感性（2/2 trained seeds 均触发），但崩溃本身是随机的。\n      Median 档审稿人接受因果方向（trained dt_emb → pathological overestimation）但质疑：\n      (a) 仅 2 seeds 的崩溃率不具统计意义；(b) self-correction 机制未解释——如果 CIVO 可以 self-correct，\n      为什么还需要干预？需要在 rebuttal 中强调：self-correction 不可靠（seed 2 eval 仅恢复到 268 = 29% baseline），\n      且 sustained vs transient overestimation 的分界点无法事先预测。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"复制 008f 因果控制（subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8）到 seed 1-2，验证无 dt_embedding 时的稳定性\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 503\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.30\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed1_trend: \"zigzag recovery 173→375→324→246→319→503\"\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 148\n      seed2_nve_105K: 1.14\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed2_trend: \"peak 359@75K then monotonic decline to 148\"\n      reward_MAE: 0.747\n      reward_MAE_vs_baseline: \"75x\"\n      cross_seed_consistency: \"poor — seed 1 recovers to 503, seed 2 declines to 148\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档的关键攻击点在 008f 的 reward_MAE（baseline 的 75x）和跨 seed 不一致性。\n      Seed 1 的 zigzag recovery 到 503（55% baseline）是合理的；seed 2 declining 到 148（16% baseline）\n      则暴露 008f 不是一个可靠的 \"保护\" 方案。审稿人会问：\"如果去掉 dt_embedding 导致 reward prediction 崩塌（MAE=0.747），\n      那么 008f 的'稳定性'是否只是因为 critic 已经无法学到有意义的值——是'保护'还是'功能丧失'？\"\n      这个质疑在 median 档是合理的——008f 的定位必须严格限制在\"因果控制实验\"（证明 dt_embedding 是 CIVO 的必要条件），\n      不能作为推荐方案。Seed 2 的 nve=1.14x@105K（borderline）也会被拿来质疑阈值的鲁棒性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008f cross-seed comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Seed 0 (s0)\", \"Seed 1\", \"Seed 2\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"eval@105K\", \"503\", \"503*\", \"148\"]\n          - [\"NVE@105K\", \"0.30\", \"0.30*\", \"1.14\"]\n          - [\"Peak eval\", \"503@105K\", \"503@105K*\", \"359@75K\"]\n          - [\"Trend\", \"zigzag recovery\", \"zigzag recovery*\", \"monotonic decline\"]\n        note: \"*seed 0 和 seed 1 实为同一 seed（deterministic reproduction），仅 seed 2 为独立 seed\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"008f seed 1 vs seed 2 eval 曲线对比，标注 reward_MAE=0.747 作为功能退化警告\"\n    analysis: >\n      008f 作为因果控制实验成功证明了 dt_embedding 是 CIVO 的必要条件（两个 seed 均未出现 nve>1.5x），\n      但跨 seed 性能差异巨大（503 vs 148），且 reward prediction 严重退化。\n      Median 档审稿人至少会标记这一点为 major weakness：causal control 的清洁度被 reward 退化污染。\n      Rebuttal 策略：承认 008f 不是方案而是诊断工具，将推荐方案指向 008e_v3（C6）或完全移除 dt_embedding（C7 after D107）。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (mitigation) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"验证 008e_v3（trained dt_emb + dt=1 imagination + subsample ON + H=15）在 seed 1-2 的 mitigation 效果\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 870\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.80\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed1_vs_baseline: \"95%\"\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 137\n      seed2_nve_105K: 3.78\n      seed2_collapse: true\n      seed2_collapse_onset: \"95K\"\n      seed2_mechanism: \"non-CIVO (eval-driven, entropy ↑, policy destabilization)\"\n      collapse_rate: \"1/2 (50%)\"\n      mitigation_verdict: \"PARTIALLY FALSIFIED\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是 median 档最关键的结果之一。dt=1 imagination 曾被假设为实用 mitigation（seed 1: 95% baseline, nve=0.80x），\n      但 seed 2 崩溃否证了该假设。审稿人会抓住两点：\n      (1) 50% 崩溃率与 008d（dt=2 imagination）的 50% 崩溃率相同——dt=1 imagination 未降低崩溃概率；\n      (2) seed 2 的崩溃机制（entropy 上升、eval 先跌、value 温和变化）与经典 CIVO 定性不同，\n      说明 trained dt_embedding 通过多条路径创造脆弱性。\n      Median 档审稿人认为这是 \"interesting observation\"（多路径脆弱性），但不够强——仅 2 seeds，\n      且两种崩溃机制的区分缺乏正式统计检验。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008e_v3 collapse dynamics comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Feature\", \"Seed 1 (healthy)\", \"Seed 2 (collapsed)\", \"008d s0 (classic CIVO)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"eval@105K\", \"870 (95% baseline)\", \"137 (15% baseline)\", \"83 (9% baseline)\"]\n          - [\"NVE@105K\", \"0.80\", \"3.78\", \"4.12\"]\n          - [\"Value trajectory\", \"monotonically rising\", \"339→384→340 (±13%)\", \"25→60→98→138 (+130%)\"]\n          - [\"Entropy@collapse\", \"-5.2 (stable)\", \"-5.2→-3.8 (rising)\", \"-3.5→-4.9 (falling)\"]\n          - [\"Collapse driver\", \"N/A\", \"eval crash → NVE spike\", \"value explosion → eval drop\"]\n          - [\"Pathway\", \"—\", \"B (IRD, policy instability)\", \"A (CIVO, value-driven)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3 panel figure: seed 1 healthy trajectory, seed 2 collapse with entropy annotation, 008d classic CIVO for contrast\"\n    analysis: >\n      C6 partially falsified 是论文的重要转折点——从 \"practical mitigation\" 转为 \"diagnostic evidence\"。\n      Median 档的 narrative 建议是将此发现框架为 \"trained dt_embedding creates vulnerability through multiple pathways\"，\n      但审稿人会认为 2 seeds 不足以可靠区分两种 pathway。\n      额外 seeds (plan_016) 的 2/4 崩溃率确认了 50% 但仍不足以做正式统计——median 档要求至少 6-8 seeds per config。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"验证 008a（subsample OFF + unexposed trained dt_emb + H=15）的值抑制和 V-recovery 模式\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 631\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.43\n      seed1_civo_alert: 0\n      seed1_trend: \"gradual rise 140→394→414→441→492→453→547→629→631\"\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 899\n      seed2_nve_105K: 0.33\n      seed2_civo_alert: 0\n      seed2_trend: \"faster convergence 311→432→608→654→534→605→819→899\"\n      cross_seed_mean_105K: 770\n      cross_seed_std: 137\n      vs_baseline_mean: \"84%\"\n      nve_range_all_seeds: \"0.33-0.93\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Unexposed trained dt_emb（subsample OFF 意味着 dt_emb 从未见过 dt>1 数据）应表现类似 untrained dt_emb：\n      NVE 抑制 + 无 CIVO。Seed 0 (778@105K)、seed 1 (631)、seed 2 (899) 均无崩溃，NVE 全程 < 1.0x。\n      但跨 seed 方差大（631-899, CV≈18%），median 档审稿人会指出：(a) 3 seeds 的均值 770±137 只能说 \"大致恢复\"，\n      precision 不够；(b) 008a 的 zigzag pattern 是 DreamerV3 的一般特征还是特定于此配置？\n      缺乏 baseline 同 seed 对照的 zigzag 频率对比。这不会是 major weakness 但会被标注。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008a cross-seed summary\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Seed 0\", \"Seed 1\", \"Seed 2\", \"Mean ± Std\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"eval@105K\", \"778\", \"631\", \"899\", \"770 ± 137\"]\n          - [\"NVE@105K\", \"0.59\", \"0.43\", \"0.33\", \"0.45 ± 0.13\"]\n          - [\"Peak eval\", \"778@105K\", \"631@105K\", \"899@105K\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"vs baseline\", \"85%\", \"69%\", \"98%\", \"84% ± 15%\"]\n          - [\"CIVO alert\", \"0\", \"0\", \"0\", \"0/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"008a 3-seed eval learning curves with IQM band, overlaid with baseline for reference\"\n    analysis: >\n      C3（untrained/unexposed dt_emb 保护）在 3 seeds 中全部确认：NVE 持续 <1.0x，无 CIVO。\n      Median 档接受 C3 的因果方向但认为 84% baseline recovery 不够有说服力——\n      \"如果最优 mitigation 还是损失 16% performance，这更像是 'less bad' 而不是 'solution'\"。\n      审稿人建议与完全移除 dt_emb 的 008f 对比成本效益。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"扩展 008e_v3 到 seed 3-4，缩窄崩溃概率估计的置信区间\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed3_eval_return_105K: 93\n      seed3_nve_peak: 4.02\n      seed3_collapse: true\n      seed3_collapse_onset: \"85K-95K\"\n      seed3_entropy_signature: \"-4.89 (falling — closer to Pathway A/CIVO)\"\n      seed4_eval_return_105K: 899\n      seed4_nve_peak: 0.99\n      seed4_collapse: false\n      collapse_rate_4seeds: \"2/4 (50%)\"\n      collapse_95CI: \"[7%, 93%] (Clopper-Pearson exact)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      4 seeds 中 2 个崩溃（s2 和 s3）、2 个存活（s1 和 s4），确认 50% 崩溃率的点估计。\n      但 Clopper-Pearson 95% CI 仍为 [7%, 93%]，审稿人正确指出这个区间太宽，无法做有意义的推断。\n      Seed 3 的崩溃（entropy 下降）看起来更接近 Pathway A（CIVO），而 seed 2（entropy 上升）是 Pathway B（IRD），\n      但 n=2 per pathway 完全不够做统计区分。\n      Median 档的核心批评：50% 崩溃率意味着 dt=1 imagination 和 dt=2 imagination 的脆弱性相同，\n      那么 \"架构边界\" 叙事的增量价值在哪里？\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008e_v3 all-seed collapse summary\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"NVE peak\", \"Collapse?\", \"Pathway\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s1\", \"870\", \"0.80\", \"No\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"137\", \"3.78\", \"Yes\", \"B (IRD, entropy ↑)\"]\n          - [\"s3\", \"93\", \"4.02\", \"Yes\", \"A-like (entropy ↓)\"]\n          - [\"s4\", \"899\", \"0.99\", \"No\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Rate\", \"—\", \"—\", \"2/4 = 50%\", \"Mixed\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-seed eval trajectory panel with collapse onset markers, color-coded by pathway type\"\n    analysis: >\n      Plan_016 的 4 seeds 收窄了估计但统计力仍不足。Median 档审稿人会标记：\n      \"4 seeds per config × 50% collapse rate = 单位实验成本下统计效率极低，\n      需要 ≥12 seeds 才能将 CI 缩窄到有意义区间 [30%, 70%]。\"\n      对 rebuttal 价值有限——确认了 50% 但无法 defend against \"statistically underpowered\"。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 imag + H=8\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"freeze dt_embedding（requires_grad=False），保持随机初始化。诊断 dt_emb 的 TRAINING 是否是 CIVO 的必要条件\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_return_105K: 204\n      nve_105K: 0.42\n      nve_range: \"0.39-0.47\"\n      collapse: false\n      actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n      actor_entropy_105K: -4.855\n      value_mean_105K: 56.2\n      gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n      failure_mode: \"gradient_starvation — actor_loss→0, critic underestimates\"\n      vs_baseline: \"22%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Frozen dt_emb 阻止了 CIVO（NVE 0.39-0.47，远低于 1.5x），确认了 dt_emb TRAINING 是 CIVO 的必要条件。\n      但引入了新失败模式：gradient starvation。随机初始化的 frozen embedding 给 RSSM 提供无信息量的 conditioning signal，\n      actor_loss→0 意味着 actor 梯度消失，策略无法有效改进。\n      Median 档审稿人会认为这是 \"expected but useful\"——frozen random embedding 当然不好用，\n      但它闭合了 2×2 消融矩阵（trained/frozen × exposed/unexposed）。\n      Novelty 评价：2.5-3.0。这个结果是消融设计的自然推论，不是独立贡献。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"dt_emb training ablation matrix\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Exposed to dt>1 (subsample ON)\", \"Unexposed (subsample OFF)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained dt_emb\", \"008d: CIVO collapse (NVE 2.09x)\", \"008a: V-recovery (NVE 0.59x)\"]\n          - [\"Frozen dt_emb\", \"015b: gradient starvation (NVE 0.42x)\", \"(= 008a equivalent, cancelled)\"]\n          - [\"No dt_emb (dim=0)\", \"008f: reward degradation (NVE 0.30x)\", \"N/A\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 消融矩阵热力图：NVE peak × eval@105K，标注每个 cell 的失败模式\"\n    analysis: >\n      015b 闭合了关键消融，但 median 档审稿人会指出矩阵的解读过度简化：\n      仅 1 seed per cell（除 008d 有多 seed），且不同 cell 的失败模式（CIVO vs gradient starvation vs reward degradation）\n      不可比——不能简单用 NVE 一个指标统一评估。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Cheetah Run cross-environment validation (plans 020-023)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"Cheetah Run dt=1 baseline，建立第二环境的 v/e calibration\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_200K: 625\n      seed1_eval_return_200K: 520\n      seed2_eval_return_200K: 645\n      cross_seed_mean: 597\n      cross_seed_std: 68\n      ve_ratio_converged: \"0.60-0.70\"\n      convergence_step: \"150K-200K\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah Run baseline 表现低于 Walker Walk（~600 vs ~950），variance 更高。\n      已有 5 seeds 数据（s0=625, s1=520, s2=645, s3=642, s4=537），均值 594±54。\n      Median 档审稿人接受 baseline 稳定性但会注意到 s4 的 194K→204K 骤降（537→302 transient drop），\n      质疑 Cheetah 基线本身的不稳定性是否混淆了 CIVO 诊断。\n      Converged v/e 约 0.60-0.70，为 NVE normalization 提供基准。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah baseline cross-seed\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"eval_final\", \"eval_peak\", \"ve_ratio_converged\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"625\", \"625\", \"~0.65\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"520\", \"573\", \"~0.60\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"645\", \"645\", \"~0.65\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"597\", \"614\", \"~0.63\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah baseline 3-seed learning curves with IQM confidence band\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 确立但 inter-seed variance（CV≈11%）高于 Walker（CV≈3%），\n      这意味着 Cheetah 的 CIVO 检测需要更多 seeds 才能达到 Walker 的统计 power。\n      Median 档审稿人会指出此 asymmetry。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"Cheetah Run 中复制 CIVO trigger（dt=2 + subsample ON + trained dt_emb）\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 1\n      seed0_nve_peak: 70.64\n      seed0_civo: true\n      seed0_collapse_type: \"catastrophic\"\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 52\n      seed1_nve_peak: 8.27\n      seed1_civo: true\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 85\n      seed2_nve_peak: 12.5\n      seed2_civo: true\n      civo_rate: \"3/3 (100%)\"\n      mean_nve_peak: 30.5\n      cheetah_vs_walker_severity: \"Cheetah CIVO severity >> Walker (mean NVE 30x vs 3x)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah 已有 2 seeds 数据（s0: NVE=70.64 catastrophic, s1/exp_010b: NVE=8.27 severe）。\n      Cheetah 的 CIVO 比 Walker 严重得多——NVE 峰值 8-70x vs Walker 的 2-4x。\n      这是因为 Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 更大（更高维运动学 → dt>1 预测更难）。\n      预测 seed 2 也会 CIVO（NVE ~10-15x），给出 3/3 = 100% 崩溃率。\n      Median 档认为这强化了 C1/C2 的跨环境泛化，但会质疑：\n      (a) Cheetah 的 CIVO 动力学与 Walker 定性不同（更早、更严重），是否真是同一机制？\n      (b) 仅 2 个环境（Walker + Cheetah）不够 claim \"generalizes\"——3 环境是最低限度。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah CIVO trigger cross-seed\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"NVE peak\", \"Collapse type\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"~1\", \"70.64\", \"catastrophic\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"52\", \"8.27\", \"severe\"]\n          - [\"s2 (predicted)\", \"~85\", \"~12.5\", \"severe\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah NVE time series 3 seeds vs Walker 3 seeds, showing environment-dependent severity\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 的 100% 崩溃率（vs Walker 50%）和更高 NVE 峰值是双刃剑：\n      强化了 CIVO 是真实威胁，但也暗示 Walker 的 50% 可能是偏低的 — 环境越难 CIVO 越强。\n      Median 档审稿人接受跨环境 CIVO 存在性但认为 severity 差异（10x）需要解释：\n      是 RSSM capacity 差异还是 task complexity 差异？\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: \"Cheetah Run 因果控制：去掉 dt_embedding 是否阻止 CIVO\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 97\n      seed0_nve_peak: 0.20\n      seed0_civo: false\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 77\n      seed1_nve_peak: 0.10\n      seed1_civo: false\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 90\n      seed2_nve_peak: 0.15\n      seed2_civo: false\n      civo_prevention_rate: \"3/3 (100%)\"\n      mean_eval_vs_baseline: \"15%\"\n      reward_MAE_vs_baseline: \">50x\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有 2 seeds：s0 eval=96.5（NVE 0.2, no CIVO），s1 eval=77.3（NVE 0.1, no CIVO）。\n      与 Walker 008f 一致：去掉 dt_embedding 完全阻止 CIVO，但 eval 严重退化（仅 ~15% baseline）。\n      Cheetah 的退化比 Walker 更严重（Walker 008f 达 55% baseline），因为 Cheetah 对 reward prediction 更敏感。\n      Median 档接受因果控制成立（5/5 across 2 environments: no dt_emb → no CIVO），\n      但再次质疑：这是 \"prevention\" 还是 \"feature removal leading to functional impairment\"？\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-environment causal control (dt_embed_dim=0)\"\n        columns: [\"Environment\", \"Seeds\", \"CIVO rate\", \"Mean eval vs baseline\", \"Reward MAE ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"3 (s0, s3, s4)\", \"0/3\", \"~40%\", \"75x\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"2-3\", \"0/3\", \"~15%\", \">50x\"]\n          - [\"Combined\", \"5-6\", \"0/5+\", \"~30%\", \">>1x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: CIVO rate and eval retention for dt_embed_dim=0 across environments\"\n    analysis: >\n      因果控制在 Cheetah 中复现，5/5 完美分离确认 dt_embedding 是 CIVO 的必要条件。\n      但 eval 退化在 Cheetah 更严重，暴露了一个 tension：去掉 dt_embedding \"治愈\" CIVO\n      但也移除了 dt-conditioning 的功能价值。这对 \"CIVO 是 dt-conditioning 不可避免的副作用\" 的叙事有利，\n      但审稿人会要求解释为什么不能 have both（有效 conditioning + 无 CIVO）。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"Cheetah Run 中验证 unexposed trained dt_emb 的值抑制效果\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 532\n      seed0_nve_105K: 0.49\n      seed0_civo: false\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 504\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.48\n      seed1_civo: false\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 480\n      seed2_nve_105K: 0.52\n      seed2_civo: false\n      mean_eval_vs_baseline: \"85%\"\n      nve_range: \"0.48-0.52\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有 2 seeds：s0=532（NVE 0.49），s1=504（NVE 0.48）。Unexposed dt_emb 在 Cheetah 中也有效：\n      NVE < 1.0x，eval 保留 ~85% baseline。与 Walker 008a 一致（84% baseline）。\n      这是 C3 跨环境验证的最强数据：两个环境的 unexposed dt_emb 均表现出值抑制 + 高 eval 保留。\n      Median 档接受 C3 但认为 \"unexposed = subsample OFF\" 只是一种 workaround，\n      不是对 CIVO 机制的根本解决。\"如果你不让模型见到 dt>1 数据，当然不会 CIVO——但这也失去了 temporal abstraction 的目的。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"C3 cross-environment: unexposed dt_emb\"\n        columns: [\"Environment\", \"Seeds\", \"Mean eval vs baseline\", \"NVE range\", \"CIVO\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"3\", \"84%\", \"0.33-0.93\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"2-3\", \"85%\", \"0.48-0.52\", \"0/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-environment eval retention bar chart: unexposed dt_emb vs baseline vs trained dt_emb\"\n    analysis: >\n      C3 获得跨环境确认（6 seeds, 0 CIVO, 84-85% baseline），是论文中最 robust 的正面结果。\n      但 median 档正确指出这不是 mitigation——它避开了问题而非解决问题。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Diagnostic analyses (plans 030-034)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: \"量化不同模型在 dt=1 和 dt=2 上的 RSSM 预测质量差距\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_obs_gap: 2.04\n      baseline_reward_gap: 1.56\n      008d_obs_gap: 1.30\n      008d_reward_gap: 2.78\n      008f_obs_gap: 2.75\n      008f_reward_gap: 1.01\n      008d_dt1_obs_MSE: 41.31\n      baseline_dt1_obs_MSE: 13.49\n      key_finding: \"008d 的低 obs gap (1.30x) 具误导性——其 dt=1 绝对误差已是 baseline 3x\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      RSSM fidelity 分析已完成（exp_rssm_fidelity_analysis）。核心发现：\n      008d 的 obs gap ratio 看起来最小（1.30x），但绝对误差最大（dt1: 41.31 vs baseline 13.49），\n      说明模型整体已崩塌，gap ratio 失去意义。008f 的 reward gap (1.01x) 说明无 dt_embedding 时\n      reward head 无法区分 dt=1/dt=2——这是 \"功能丧失\" 不是 \"改善\"。\n      Median 档审稿人认为这是 \"expected and confirmatory\"——RSSM 在 dt>1 预测不好是已知的，\n      novelty 不在发现本身而在它与 CIVO 的因果连接。但审稿人会质疑：\n      只有 1 个 checkpoint 的分析，如何确认这是训练全程的 pattern 而非特定 step 的 artifact？\n    tables:\n      - name: \"RSSM Fidelity Table\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"dt1 obs_MSE\", \"dt2 obs_MSE\", \"obs gap\", \"dt1 reward_MAE\", \"dt2 reward_MAE\", \"reward gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"baseline\", \"13.49\", \"27.50\", \"2.04x\", \"0.0102\", \"0.0159\", \"1.56x\"]\n          - [\"008d (trained dt_emb)\", \"41.31\", \"53.67\", \"1.30x\", \"0.0568\", \"0.1579\", \"2.78x\"]\n          - [\"008f (no dt_emb)\", \"8.01\", \"22.04\", \"2.75x\", \"0.7469\", \"0.7526\", \"1.01x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart with both absolute values and ratios side-by-side, preventing ratio-only misleading\"\n    analysis: >\n      RSSM fidelity 分析确认了机制假说但未超越 \"supporting evidence\"。\n      Median 档给这个分析 moderate credit 但不视为独立贡献。\n      建议在 rebuttal 中加入训练过程中 fidelity 的演化曲线（多 checkpoint），回应 \"single snapshot\" 质疑。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: \"对比健康 vs 崩溃配置的 actor entropy 演化\"\n    expected_results:\n      healthy_008a_entropy_trend: \"稳定在 -4.5 to -5.2 范围\"\n      healthy_008c_entropy_trend: \"缓慢下降 -3.5 → -4.8\"\n      collapsed_006_entropy_trend: \"下降后回弹 -3.5 → -4.9 → -3.8\"\n      collapsed_008d_entropy_trend: \"持续下降 -1.9 → -4.9\"\n      collapsed_008e_v3_s2_entropy_trend: \"先降后升 -5.2 → -3.8 (反常)\"\n      pathway_A_signature: \"entropy ↓ (policy 过度确定化)\"\n      pathway_B_signature: \"entropy ↑ (policy destabilization)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Actor entropy 分析是区分 Pathway A (CIVO) 和 Pathway B (IRD) 的关键诊断工具。\n      经典 CIVO (008d): value overestimate → actor exploit → entropy 下降 → 策略变得过度确定。\n      非 CIVO 崩溃 (008e_v3_s2): eval 先跌 → value 滞后 → entropy 上升 → 策略变得随机。\n      Median 档认为这是 \"useful characterization\" 但不是 \"novel contribution\"——\n      entropy 作为策略健康度指标是标准做法，两种 pathway 的区分缺乏 formal framework。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Entropy trajectory comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Config\", \"Entropy@35K\", \"Entropy@55K\", \"Entropy@85K\", \"Entropy@105K\", \"Pathway\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"008a s0 (healthy)\", \"-4.2\", \"-4.5\", \"-4.8\", \"-5.0\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"008d s0 (CIVO)\", \"-3.5\", \"-4.9\", \"—\", \"—\", \"A\"]\n          - [\"008e_v3 s2 (IRD)\", \"-3.5\", \"-5.1\", \"-5.2\", \"-3.8\", \"B\"]\n          - [\"016e (SGS)\", \"-2.1\", \"-3.6\", \"-4.3\", \"—\", \"A (delayed)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Entropy vs step: healthy configs (blue band) vs CIVO (red, entropy ↓) vs IRD (orange, entropy ↑)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Entropy 分析确认两种崩溃 pathway 的存在，但 n=1-2 per pathway 不足以 formalize。\n      Median 档审稿人建议：如果要将 dual-pathway 作为贡献，需要至少 5 seeds per pathway 并做 statistical test。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: \"V(s) vs Monte Carlo return 分布对比\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_dt_emb_divergence: \"V(s) 分布右偏移 + 重尾，MC return 集中在低区间\"\n      untrained_dt_emb_match: \"V(s) 和 MC return 分布大致重叠，V(s) 略微左移\"\n      collapsed_state: \"V(s) 均值远超 MC return p95，完全脱钩\"\n      healthy_calibration: \"V(s) 中位数在 MC return IQR 内\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是对 v/e ratio proxy 的补充验证。直接展示 V(s) 分布 vs 实际回报分布比单一 ratio 更具信息量。\n      Median 档审稿人在 R3 中质疑 v/e ratio 是 crude proxy——这个分析直接回应。\n      预期结果：trained dt_emb 的 V(s) 明显偏高且扩散，untrained 的则接近校准。\n      但审稿人仍会指出：MC return 在 imagination 中不可直接计算（需要 ground truth environment），\n      只能用 eval return 作为 proxy，引入额外近似误差。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 violin plot panel: (trained/untrained) × (pre-collapse/post-collapse), V(s) distribution in orange vs MC return in blue\"\n    analysis: >\n      Distributional 分析增加了 R3 的防御深度，但实现依赖 eval return 作为 MC return proxy，\n      审稿人可能认为这只是换了一种方式展示同样的信息。Median 档给 minor positive credit。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: \"分析 dt=1 和 dt=2 embedding 向量的演化\"\n    expected_results:\n      initial_cosine_sim: \"~0.0 (random init)\"\n      trained_25K_cosine_sim: \"~0.3\"\n      trained_55K_cosine_sim: \"~0.65\"\n      trained_105K_cosine_sim: \"~0.75 (converging)\"\n      l2_distance_trend: \"monotonically increasing\"\n      frozen_cosine_sim: \"constant at ~0.0\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trained dt_embedding 的 dt=1 和 dt=2 向量会在训练过程中逐渐分离（cosine sim 从 ~0 增加，\n      但 L2 距离增加），说明 embedding 学到了 dt-specific representation。\n      Frozen embedding 保持初始状态不变（cosine sim ≈ 0）。\n      Median 档认为这是 \"descriptive visualization\"——确认 embedding 在训练，但不提供超越已知的 insight。\n      审稿人的反应：nice plot, but what does it tell us that we didn't already know from the gradient analysis?\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: cosine similarity between dt=1 and dt=2 embedding vectors over training steps, for trained vs frozen\"\n    analysis: >\n      Low priority（P2）合理。Cosine similarity 分析提供视觉直觉但不支撑任何独立 claim。\n      Median 档中这会出现在 appendix 如果提交，不会影响评分。\n\n  - name: \"NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_034\"\n    description: \"在不同阈值（1.3x, 1.5x, 1.7x, 2.0x）下计算分类准确率和 AUROC\"\n    expected_results:\n      threshold_1.3x_accuracy: 0.86\n      threshold_1.5x_accuracy: 0.93\n      threshold_1.7x_accuracy: 0.90\n      threshold_2.0x_accuracy: 0.83\n      youden_optimal_threshold: 1.53\n      AUROC_walker: 0.98\n      AUROC_cheetah: 0.95\n      AUROC_combined: 0.969\n      AUROC_bootstrap_95CI: \"[0.91, 1.00]\"\n      n_total_datapoints: 29\n      leave_one_env_out_AUROC_walker_train: 0.97\n      leave_one_env_out_AUROC_cheetah_test: 0.92\n    result_rationale: >\n      NVE 阈值分析基于所有可用 seeds（~29 数据点跨 4 环境）。1.5x 是 near-optimal（Youden index 收敛到 1.53x），\n      AUROC 0.969 表明 NVE 是 strong discriminator。\n      但 median 档审稿人一致标记（Dream D8）：阈值在同数据集上 calibrate 和 validate = in-sample bias。\n      Leave-one-environment-out CV 部分回应这个问题（Cheetah 作为 held-out 时 AUROC 仍 ~0.92），\n      但只有 2 个环境做 LOO-CV 统计意义有限。\n      Bootstrap 95% CI [0.91, 1.00] 看起来 impressive 但样本量小时 bootstrap CI 本身偏乐观。\n      这是 median 档的核心方法论弱点之一。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"NVE threshold ROC analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Threshold\", \"Sensitivity\", \"Specificity\", \"Accuracy\", \"Youden J\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"1.3x\", \"0.94\", \"0.80\", \"0.86\", \"0.74\"]\n          - [\"1.5x\", \"0.88\", \"1.00\", \"0.93\", \"0.88\"]\n          - [\"1.53x (optimal)\", \"0.88\", \"1.00\", \"0.93\", \"0.88\"]\n          - [\"1.7x\", \"0.81\", \"1.00\", \"0.90\", \"0.81\"]\n          - [\"2.0x\", \"0.69\", \"1.00\", \"0.83\", \"0.69\"]\n      - name: \"Leave-one-environment-out AUROC\"\n        columns: [\"Train env\", \"Test env\", \"AUROC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker\", \"Cheetah\", \"0.92\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"Walker\", \"0.97\"]\n          - [\"Combined\", \"Combined (bootstrap)\", \"0.969 [0.91, 1.00]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ROC curve with 95% bootstrap CI band, marking Youden-optimal threshold\"\n    analysis: >\n      AUROC 0.969 是 C2 的最强定量结果，但 in-sample calibration 和 n=29 是不可回避的限制。\n      Median 档审稿人接受 NVE 作为 diagnostic tool 但不接受 1.5x 作为 generalizable threshold。\n      Rebuttal 策略：承认 limitation，强调 leave-one-env-out 结果（虽然 n 小但方向正确），\n      将 NVE threshold generalization 定位为 future work。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Cartpole Swingup (plans 050-052) — third environment\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_050\"\n    description: \"第三个 DMC 环境的 dt=1 baseline，扩展到非 locomotion 任务\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_500K: 860\n      seed1_eval_return_500K: 845\n      seed2_eval_return_500K: 870\n      cross_seed_mean: 858\n      cross_seed_std: 13\n      ve_ratio_converged: \"0.65-0.75\"\n      convergence_step: \"80K-120K\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole Swingup 是 DMC 中相对简单的任务，DreamerV3 baseline 应快速收敛到 ~850-870。\n      Inter-seed variance 预计低于 Cheetah（simpler dynamics → more consistent learning）。\n      v/e ratio 收敛到 0.65-0.75，与 Walker/Cheetah 一致。\n      Median 档审稿人认为加入第三个环境是正面的（从 \"minimum viable\" 的 3 环境升级），\n      但 Cartpole 作为相对简单任务可能不够挑战性——\"如果 CIVO 在简单任务上弱或不出现，\n      这削弱了 generalization claim 而非加强。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole baseline\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"eval@500K\", \"ve_ratio_converged\", \"convergence_step\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"860\", \"0.70\", \"100K\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"845\", \"0.68\", \"110K\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"870\", \"0.72\", \"90K\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole baseline learning curves, 3 seeds with confidence band\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 稳定。关键问题是 CIVO 在 Cartpole 的表现——如果弱于 Walker/Cheetah，\n      会被解读为 \"CIVO severity is task-dependent\"（median 档认可的弱化叙事）。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_051\"\n    description: \"Cartpole Swingup 中复制 CIVO trigger\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 520\n      seed0_nve_peak: 2.8\n      seed0_civo: true\n      seed0_collapse_type: \"partial — degradation without catastrophic collapse\"\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 680\n      seed1_nve_peak: 1.8\n      seed1_civo: true\n      seed1_collapse_type: \"mild — NVE borderline, eval recovers\"\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 350\n      seed2_nve_peak: 4.1\n      seed2_civo: true\n      seed2_collapse_type: \"moderate — sustained degradation\"\n      civo_rate: \"3/3 (NVE > 1.5x)\"\n      catastrophic_collapse_rate: \"0/3 (no complete collapse to random policy)\"\n      mean_eval_vs_baseline: \"60%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole 比 Cheetah 简单但比 Walker 的 observation space 更低维（5 vs 24 dim），\n      RSSM 在 dt>1 的预测误差相对较小。预期 CIVO 出现（NVE > 1.5x）但严重程度低于 Walker/Cheetah：\n      degradation 而非 catastrophic collapse。这是因为 Cartpole 的值函数 landscape 更平滑，\n      value overestimation 更容易被 self-correction 机制缓解。\n      Median 档审稿人会抓住这一点：\"CIVO severity 与任务复杂度相关——在简单任务上是 nuisance，\n      在复杂任务上才是 fatal。这限制了 diagnostic 的实际影响力。\"\n      但也会认可：CIVO 在所有 3 个环境中都出现（NVE > 1.5x），direction 一致。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-environment CIVO severity\"\n        columns: [\"Environment\", \"CIVO rate\", \"Mean NVE peak\", \"Catastrophic collapse rate\", \"Mean eval retention\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"2/4 (50%)\", \"2.7\", \"2/4\", \"47%\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"3/3 (100%)\", \"30.5\", \"2/3\", \"5%\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"3/3 (100%)\", \"2.9\", \"0/3\", \"60%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-environment CIVO heatmap: environment × seed, colored by NVE peak\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole 确认 CIVO 的 universality 但暴露了 severity 的强环境依赖性。\n      Median 档审稿人将此解读为 \"the phenomenon is real but its practical impact is task-dependent\"，\n      进一步将 novelty 定位为 incremental observation 而非 general finding。\n      NVE 阈值 1.5x 在 Cartpole 中仍有效（3/3 detection），增强了跨环境泛化的证据。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_052\"\n    description: \"Cartpole Swingup 因果控制（无 dt_embedding）\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 650\n      seed0_nve_peak: 0.35\n      seed0_civo: false\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 620\n      seed1_nve_peak: 0.40\n      seed1_civo: false\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 660\n      seed2_nve_peak: 0.30\n      seed2_civo: false\n      civo_prevention_rate: \"3/3 (100%)\"\n      mean_eval_vs_baseline: \"75%\"\n      reward_MAE_vs_baseline: \"~30x\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      无 dt_embedding 应阻止 CIVO（与 Walker/Cheetah 一致）。Cartpole 的 eval 保留（75%）\n      介于 Walker（40-55%）和 baseline 之间，因为 Cartpole 的 reward 结构更简单，\n      reward prediction 退化的影响相对较小。\n      Median 档审稿人：因果控制在第三个环境确认，累计 8/8 across 3 environments（no dt_emb → no CIVO）。\n      这是论文中最 robust 的因果结论之一。\n      但评论：\"因果控制只证明 dt_embedding 是 necessary condition，没有提供 mitigation pathway。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-environment causal control summary (final)\"\n        columns: [\"Environment\", \"Seeds\", \"CIVO prevented\", \"Eval retention\", \"Reward degradation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"3\", \"3/3\", \"40-55%\", \"75x MAE\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"2-3\", \"2-3/2-3\", \"~15%\", \">50x MAE\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"3\", \"3/3\", \"~75%\", \"~30x MAE\"]\n          - [\"**Total**\", \"**8-9**\", \"**8-9/8-9**\", \"**varies**\", \"**>>1x**\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar chart: eval retention by environment for dt_embed_dim=0\"\n    analysis: >\n      8/8+ 因果控制是 C2 的最终定量支撑。但 eval retention 的环境依赖性（15%-75%）\n      意味着 \"removing dt_embedding\" 的代价不一致，进一步说明 CIVO 问题没有 one-size-fits-all solution。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Advanced interventions (plan_060)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot (Walker Walk, 1 seed)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_060\"\n    description: \"监控 imagination rollout 中的 RSSM 预测不确定性，超过阈值时截断\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_return_105K: 380\n      nve_peak: 1.8\n      civo_delayed: true\n      civo_prevented: false\n      truncation_rate_avg: \"40% of rollout steps truncated\"\n      effective_horizon: \"H_eff ≈ 9 (from H=15)\"\n      eval_vs_baseline: \"41%\"\n      eval_vs_008d: \"2.7x better than 008d collapse\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Uncertainty-gated truncation 在概念上是对的（截断不确定预测避免 error compounding），\n      但在 DreamerV3 的 RSSM 中面临两个问题：\n      (1) RSSM 的 posterior entropy 不是 calibrated 的 uncertainty estimate——\n      高 entropy 可能反映 genuine uncertainty 也可能反映 poor representation；\n      (2) 截断降低了 effective horizon，相当于变相回到 H=8 的配置（已知性能较差）。\n      预测结果：CIVO 延迟但不完全阻止（NVE 仍达 1.8x），eval 中等（380 ≈ 41% baseline）。\n      Median 档审稿人：interesting pilot 但 1 seed 不足以 draw conclusions。\n      This could strengthen the intervention hierarchy as a 4th level (model-level gating)\n      but needs more work to be publishable.\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Intervention hierarchy with uncertainty gating\"\n        columns: [\"Level\", \"Method\", \"Success rate\", \"Mechanism\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"L1: Gradient\", \"SGS variants\", \"1/17\", \"Backward-pass insufficient\"]\n          - [\"L2: Output\", \"RAVE\", \"0/2\", \"EMA anchor polluted\"]\n          - [\"L3: Representation\", \"TCN\", \"2/8\", \"Narrow dose window\"]\n          - [\"L4: Model (new)\", \"Uncertainty truncation\", \"0/1 (pilot)\", \"Effective horizon reduction\"]\n          - [\"Control\", \"dt_emb removal\", \"8/8+\", \"Feature removal\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Truncation rate over training steps, overlaid with NVE and eval curves\"\n    analysis: >\n      Pilot 结果不够强支撑独立 claim，但为 intervention hierarchy 添加第四层。\n      Median 档中这会被定位为 \"preliminary evidence\" 放在 Discussion 中。\n      审稿人评价：interesting direction，please extend in camera-ready。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Hopper Hop (plan_040) — stretch goal\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: \"第三个 locomotion DMC 环境，3 configs (baseline, CIVO trigger, causal control) × 3 seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_mean_200K: 280\n      baseline_std: 45\n      civo_trigger_civo_rate: \"2/3\"\n      civo_trigger_mean_nve_peak: 5.2\n      civo_trigger_mean_eval_vs_baseline: \"25%\"\n      causal_control_civo_rate: \"0/3\"\n      causal_control_mean_eval_vs_baseline: \"35%\"\n      total_gpu_hours: 45\n    result_rationale: >\n      Hopper Hop 是比 Walker Walk 更难的 locomotion 任务（DreamerV3 baseline ~250-300）。\n      CIVO 预计出现但环境本身的 high variance 和 lower baseline 使 NVE normalization 更嘈杂。\n      2/3 崩溃率（比 Cheetah 的 3/3 低）因为 Hopper 的 value landscape 有不同 topology。\n      Median 档审稿人：第四个环境加强了 generalization 但仍是 DMC proprioceptive setting——\n      \"all four environments are DMC proprioceptive, how do we know this isn't a DMC-specific artifact?\"\n      Pixel observation 的缺失仍是 core weakness (Dream D9)。\n      45 GPU hours 的预算对 P2 priority 可能不被分配——median 档假设这个实验可能不做。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Four-environment CIVO summary\"\n        columns: [\"Environment\", \"Obs dim\", \"Baseline\", \"CIVO rate\", \"Causal control rate\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"24\", \"~950\", \"2/4 (50%)\", \"0/8 (0%)\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"17\", \"~600\", \"3/3 (100%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"5\", \"~860\", \"3/3 (100%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\"]\n          - [\"Hopper Hop\", \"15\", \"~280\", \"2/3 (67%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\"]\n          - [\"**Total**\", \"—\", \"—\", \"**10/13 (77%)**\", \"**0/17 (0%)**\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-environment radar chart: CIVO rate, severity, eval retention, causal control effectiveness\"\n    analysis: >\n      Hopper 的加入使总 CIVO detection 达 10/13（77%）和因果控制 0/17（100% prevention）。\n      但 median 档审稿人的核心攻击不在环境数量而在环境多样性：\n      全部 4 个都是 DMC continuous control + proprioceptive observation + RSSM。\n      要 \"truly generalize\" 需要不同 world model（IRIS/TWM）或 pixel observation。\n      此实验在 median 档中被视为 \"nice to have\" 而非 \"changes the verdict\"。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":764,"cache_read_input_tokens":82591,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":764},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e378428-3718-4c03-8413-20c57e8b82cc","uuid":"0c460f90-91a9-441e-b126-1e31f044267e"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":629105,"duration_api_ms":630810,"num_turns":6,"result":"Now I have all the data needed. Let me compile the comprehensive median-tier predictions.\n\n```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  部分假设未完全验证，需调整 claims 强度并补充实验。具体：(1) MPC/imagination 架构边界从 \"novel finding\" 弱化为 \"empirical observation consistent with architectural dependency\"，Discussion 中加入 TAWM 设定差异的详细对比表（obs space / planning horizon / critic structure / dt range），明确哪些 confounds 未控制；(2) 梯度-因果解耦从独立贡献降级为 C7 的 supporting analysis，不在 abstract/intro 中突出；(3) 补充 ensemble critic 快速消融——在 DreamerV3 critic 上加 2-head ensemble + min-Q，即使简化版也堵住 R9 的 \"没试过标准对策\" 攻击（预计 1-2 天 GPU，2 seeds，Walker 单环境）；(4) NVE 讨论加入 leave-one-environment-out cross-validation AUROC（已有 4 环境数据可离线计算）+ bootstrap 95% CI；(5) 论文标题考虑从 \"Diagnosing...\" 改为 \"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails...\" 以降低 novelty 期望值。Rebuttal 可将 borderline 翻转但需额外 2-3 天实验。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # Walker Walk multi-seed replication (plans 011-016)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"复制 008d 配置（subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8）到 seed 1 和 seed 2，验证 CIVO 崩溃的跨 seed 可复现性\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 131\n      seed1_nve_peak: 4.12\n      seed1_nve_peak_step: 55K\n      seed1_collapse: true\n      seed1_collapse_onset: 25K\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 268\n      seed2_nve_peak: 2.05\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 25K\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed2_self_correction: true\n      seed2_nve_105K: 0.38\n      collapse_rate: \"1/2 (50%)\"\n      nve_gt_1.5x_rate: \"2/2 (100%)\"\n      nve_threshold_separation: \"4/4 perfect (trained 2/2 > 1.5x, untrained 0/2 < 1.5x)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档认可 nve>1.5x 阈值的 4/4 分离力作为诊断工具，但对崩溃率 50%（仅 2 个独立 seed）的统计 power 提出质疑。\n      Seed 1 重现经典 CIVO（value 爆炸 → eval 下降），seed 2 自我修正（transient nve>1.5x → 回落）。\n      审稿人会指出：2 seeds 只能给出 50% 的点估计，95% CI 覆盖 [7%, 93%]（Clopper-Pearson），无法区分 \"rare event\" 和 \"coin flip\"。\n      这是 median 档 major weakness #1：per-method 样本量不足。Full SGS 仅 3 seeds、RAVE 仅 2 configs 同样被标记。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008d cross-seed NVE trajectory\"\n        columns: [\"Step\", \"Seed 0 NVE\", \"Seed 1 NVE\", \"Seed 2 NVE\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"25K\", \"1.78\", \"1.78\", \"2.05\"]\n          - [\"35K\", \"1.71\", \"1.71\", \"1.24\"]\n          - [\"45K\", \"2.09\", \"2.09\", \"1.62\"]\n          - [\"55K\", \"4.12\", \"4.12\", \"1.41\"]\n          - [\"65K\", \"-\", \"1.23\", \"0.94\"]\n          - [\"85K\", \"-\", \"1.15\", \"0.51\"]\n          - [\"105K\", \"-\", \"1.57\", \"0.38\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NVE 时间序列图：3 seeds 并排，标注 1.5x 阈值线。Seed 0/1 持续超阈值，seed 2 transient 后回落。\"\n    analysis: >\n      CIVO 诊断标记（nve>1.5x）具有 100% 敏感性（2/2 trained seeds 均触发），但崩溃本身是随机的。\n      Median 档审稿人接受因果方向（trained dt_emb → pathological overestimation）但质疑：\n      (a) 仅 2 seeds 的崩溃率不具统计意义；(b) self-correction 机制未解释——如果 CIVO 可以 self-correct，\n      为什么还需要干预？需要在 rebuttal 中强调：self-correction 不可靠（seed 2 eval 仅恢复到 268 = 29% baseline），\n      且 sustained vs transient overestimation 的分界点无法事先预测。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"复制 008f 因果控制（subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8）到 seed 1-2，验证无 dt_embedding 时的稳定性\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 503\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.30\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed1_trend: \"zigzag recovery 173→375→324→246→319→503\"\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 148\n      seed2_nve_105K: 1.14\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed2_trend: \"peak 359@75K then monotonic decline to 148\"\n      reward_MAE: 0.747\n      reward_MAE_vs_baseline: \"75x\"\n      cross_seed_consistency: \"poor — seed 1 recovers to 503, seed 2 declines to 148\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档的关键攻击点在 008f 的 reward_MAE（baseline 的 75x）和跨 seed 不一致性。\n      Seed 1 的 zigzag recovery 到 503（55% baseline）是合理的；seed 2 declining 到 148（16% baseline）\n      则暴露 008f 不是一个可靠的 \"保护\" 方案。审稿人会问：\"如果去掉 dt_embedding 导致 reward prediction 崩塌（MAE=0.747），\n      那么 008f 的'稳定性'是否只是因为 critic 已经无法学到有意义的值——是'保护'还是'功能丧失'？\"\n      这个质疑在 median 档是合理的——008f 的定位必须严格限制在\"因果控制实验\"（证明 dt_embedding 是 CIVO 的必要条件），\n      不能作为推荐方案。Seed 2 的 nve=1.14x@105K（borderline）也会被拿来质疑阈值的鲁棒性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008f cross-seed comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Seed 0 (s0)\", \"Seed 1\", \"Seed 2\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"eval@105K\", \"503\", \"503*\", \"148\"]\n          - [\"NVE@105K\", \"0.30\", \"0.30*\", \"1.14\"]\n          - [\"Peak eval\", \"503@105K\", \"503@105K*\", \"359@75K\"]\n          - [\"Trend\", \"zigzag recovery\", \"zigzag recovery*\", \"monotonic decline\"]\n        note: \"*seed 0 和 seed 1 实为同一 seed（deterministic reproduction），仅 seed 2 为独立 seed\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"008f seed 1 vs seed 2 eval 曲线对比，标注 reward_MAE=0.747 作为功能退化警告\"\n    analysis: >\n      008f 作为因果控制实验成功证明了 dt_embedding 是 CIVO 的必要条件（两个 seed 均未出现 nve>1.5x），\n      但跨 seed 性能差异巨大（503 vs 148），且 reward prediction 严重退化。\n      Median 档审稿人至少会标记这一点为 major weakness：causal control 的清洁度被 reward 退化污染。\n      Rebuttal 策略：承认 008f 不是方案而是诊断工具，将推荐方案指向 008e_v3（C6）或完全移除 dt_embedding（C7 after D107）。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (mitigation) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"验证 008e_v3（trained dt_emb + dt=1 imagination + subsample ON + H=15）在 seed 1-2 的 mitigation 效果\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 870\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.80\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed1_vs_baseline: \"95%\"\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 137\n      seed2_nve_105K: 3.78\n      seed2_collapse: true\n      seed2_collapse_onset: \"95K\"\n      seed2_mechanism: \"non-CIVO (eval-driven, entropy ↑, policy destabilization)\"\n      collapse_rate: \"1/2 (50%)\"\n      mitigation_verdict: \"PARTIALLY FALSIFIED\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是 median 档最关键的结果之一。dt=1 imagination 曾被假设为实用 mitigation（seed 1: 95% baseline, nve=0.80x），\n      但 seed 2 崩溃否证了该假设。审稿人会抓住两点：\n      (1) 50% 崩溃率与 008d（dt=2 imagination）的 50% 崩溃率相同——dt=1 imagination 未降低崩溃概率；\n      (2) seed 2 的崩溃机制（entropy 上升、eval 先跌、value 温和变化）与经典 CIVO 定性不同，\n      说明 trained dt_embedding 通过多条路径创造脆弱性。\n      Median 档审稿人认为这是 \"interesting observation\"（多路径脆弱性），但不够强——仅 2 seeds，\n      且两种崩溃机制的区分缺乏正式统计检验。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008e_v3 collapse dynamics comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Feature\", \"Seed 1 (healthy)\", \"Seed 2 (collapsed)\", \"008d s0 (classic CIVO)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"eval@105K\", \"870 (95% baseline)\", \"137 (15% baseline)\", \"83 (9% baseline)\"]\n          - [\"NVE@105K\", \"0.80\", \"3.78\", \"4.12\"]\n          - [\"Value trajectory\", \"monotonically rising\", \"339→384→340 (±13%)\", \"25→60→98→138 (+130%)\"]\n          - [\"Entropy@collapse\", \"-5.2 (stable)\", \"-5.2→-3.8 (rising)\", \"-3.5→-4.9 (falling)\"]\n          - [\"Collapse driver\", \"N/A\", \"eval crash → NVE spike\", \"value explosion → eval drop\"]\n          - [\"Pathway\", \"—\", \"B (IRD, policy instability)\", \"A (CIVO, value-driven)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3 panel figure: seed 1 healthy trajectory, seed 2 collapse with entropy annotation, 008d classic CIVO for contrast\"\n    analysis: >\n      C6 partially falsified 是论文的重要转折点——从 \"practical mitigation\" 转为 \"diagnostic evidence\"。\n      Median 档的 narrative 建议是将此发现框架为 \"trained dt_embedding creates vulnerability through multiple pathways\"，\n      但审稿人会认为 2 seeds 不足以可靠区分两种 pathway。\n      额外 seeds (plan_016) 的 2/4 崩溃率确认了 50% 但仍不足以做正式统计——median 档要求至少 6-8 seeds per config。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"验证 008a（subsample OFF + unexposed trained dt_emb + H=15）的值抑制和 V-recovery 模式\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 631\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.43\n      seed1_civo_alert: 0\n      seed1_trend: \"gradual rise 140→394→414→441→492→453→547→629→631\"\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 899\n      seed2_nve_105K: 0.33\n      seed2_civo_alert: 0\n      seed2_trend: \"faster convergence 311→432→608→654→534→605→819→899\"\n      cross_seed_mean_105K: 770\n      cross_seed_std: 137\n      vs_baseline_mean: \"84%\"\n      nve_range_all_seeds: \"0.33-0.93\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Unexposed trained dt_emb（subsample OFF 意味着 dt_emb 从未见过 dt>1 数据）应表现类似 untrained dt_emb：\n      NVE 抑制 + 无 CIVO。Seed 0 (778@105K)、seed 1 (631)、seed 2 (899) 均无崩溃，NVE 全程 < 1.0x。\n      但跨 seed 方差大（631-899, CV≈18%），median 档审稿人会指出：(a) 3 seeds 的均值 770±137 只能说 \"大致恢复\"，\n      precision 不够；(b) 008a 的 zigzag pattern 是 DreamerV3 的一般特征还是特定于此配置？\n      缺乏 baseline 同 seed 对照的 zigzag 频率对比。这不会是 major weakness 但会被标注。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008a cross-seed summary\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Seed 0\", \"Seed 1\", \"Seed 2\", \"Mean ± Std\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"eval@105K\", \"778\", \"631\", \"899\", \"770 ± 137\"]\n          - [\"NVE@105K\", \"0.59\", \"0.43\", \"0.33\", \"0.45 ± 0.13\"]\n          - [\"Peak eval\", \"778@105K\", \"631@105K\", \"899@105K\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"vs baseline\", \"85%\", \"69%\", \"98%\", \"84% ± 15%\"]\n          - [\"CIVO alert\", \"0\", \"0\", \"0\", \"0/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"008a 3-seed eval learning curves with IQM band, overlaid with baseline for reference\"\n    analysis: >\n      C3（untrained/unexposed dt_emb 保护）在 3 seeds 中全部确认：NVE 持续 <1.0x，无 CIVO。\n      Median 档接受 C3 的因果方向但认为 84% baseline recovery 不够有说服力——\n      \"如果最优 mitigation 还是损失 16% performance，这更像是 'less bad' 而不是 'solution'\"。\n      审稿人建议与完全移除 dt_emb 的 008f 对比成本效益。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"扩展 008e_v3 到 seed 3-4，缩窄崩溃概率估计的置信区间\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed3_eval_return_105K: 93\n      seed3_nve_peak: 4.02\n      seed3_collapse: true\n      seed3_collapse_onset: \"85K-95K\"\n      seed3_entropy_signature: \"-4.89 (falling — closer to Pathway A/CIVO)\"\n      seed4_eval_return_105K: 899\n      seed4_nve_peak: 0.99\n      seed4_collapse: false\n      collapse_rate_4seeds: \"2/4 (50%)\"\n      collapse_95CI: \"[7%, 93%] (Clopper-Pearson exact)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      4 seeds 中 2 个崩溃（s2 和 s3）、2 个存活（s1 和 s4），确认 50% 崩溃率的点估计。\n      但 Clopper-Pearson 95% CI 仍为 [7%, 93%]，审稿人正确指出这个区间太宽，无法做有意义的推断。\n      Seed 3 的崩溃（entropy 下降）看起来更接近 Pathway A（CIVO），而 seed 2（entropy 上升）是 Pathway B（IRD），\n      但 n=2 per pathway 完全不够做统计区分。\n      Median 档的核心批评：50% 崩溃率意味着 dt=1 imagination 和 dt=2 imagination 的脆弱性相同，\n      那么 \"架构边界\" 叙事的增量价值在哪里？\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008e_v3 all-seed collapse summary\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"NVE peak\", \"Collapse?\", \"Pathway\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s1\", \"870\", \"0.80\", \"No\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"137\", \"3.78\", \"Yes\", \"B (IRD, entropy ↑)\"]\n          - [\"s3\", \"93\", \"4.02\", \"Yes\", \"A-like (entropy ↓)\"]\n          - [\"s4\", \"899\", \"0.99\", \"No\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Rate\", \"—\", \"—\", \"2/4 = 50%\", \"Mixed\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-seed eval trajectory panel with collapse onset markers, color-coded by pathway type\"\n    analysis: >\n      Plan_016 的 4 seeds 收窄了估计但统计力仍不足。Median 档审稿人会标记：\n      \"4 seeds per config × 50% collapse rate = 单位实验成本下统计效率极低，\n      需要 ≥12 seeds 才能将 CI 缩窄到有意义区间 [30%, 70%]。\"\n      对 rebuttal 价值有限——确认了 50% 但无法 defend against \"statistically underpowered\"。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 imag + H=8\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"freeze dt_embedding（requires_grad=False），保持随机初始化。诊断 dt_emb 的 TRAINING 是否是 CIVO 的必要条件\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_return_105K: 204\n      nve_105K: 0.42\n      nve_range: \"0.39-0.47\"\n      collapse: false\n      actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n      actor_entropy_105K: -4.855\n      value_mean_105K: 56.2\n      gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n      failure_mode: \"gradient_starvation — actor_loss→0, critic underestimates\"\n      vs_baseline: \"22%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Frozen dt_emb 阻止了 CIVO（NVE 0.39-0.47，远低于 1.5x），确认了 dt_emb TRAINING 是 CIVO 的必要条件。\n      但引入了新失败模式：gradient starvation。随机初始化的 frozen embedding 给 RSSM 提供无信息量的 conditioning signal，\n      actor_loss→0 意味着 actor 梯度消失，策略无法有效改进。\n      Median 档审稿人会认为这是 \"expected but useful\"——frozen random embedding 当然不好用，\n      但它闭合了 2×2 消融矩阵（trained/frozen × exposed/unexposed）。\n      Novelty 评价：2.5-3.0。这个结果是消融设计的自然推论，不是独立贡献。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"dt_emb training ablation matrix\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Exposed to dt>1 (subsample ON)\", \"Unexposed (subsample OFF)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained dt_emb\", \"008d: CIVO collapse (NVE 2.09x)\", \"008a: V-recovery (NVE 0.59x)\"]\n          - [\"Frozen dt_emb\", \"015b: gradient starvation (NVE 0.42x)\", \"(= 008a equivalent, cancelled)\"]\n          - [\"No dt_emb (dim=0)\", \"008f: reward degradation (NVE 0.30x)\", \"N/A\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 消融矩阵热力图：NVE peak × eval@105K，标注每个 cell 的失败模式\"\n    analysis: >\n      015b 闭合了关键消融，但 median 档审稿人会指出矩阵的解读过度简化：\n      仅 1 seed per cell（除 008d 有多 seed），且不同 cell 的失败模式（CIVO vs gradient starvation vs reward degradation）\n      不可比——不能简单用 NVE 一个指标统一评估。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Cheetah Run cross-environment validation (plans 020-023)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"Cheetah Run dt=1 baseline，建立第二环境的 v/e calibration\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_200K: 625\n      seed1_eval_return_200K: 520\n      seed2_eval_return_200K: 645\n      cross_seed_mean: 597\n      cross_seed_std: 68\n      ve_ratio_converged: \"0.60-0.70\"\n      convergence_step: \"150K-200K\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah Run baseline 表现低于 Walker Walk（~600 vs ~950），variance 更高。\n      已有 5 seeds 数据（s0=625, s1=520, s2=645, s3=642, s4=537），均值 594±54。\n      Median 档审稿人接受 baseline 稳定性但会注意到 s4 的 194K→204K 骤降（537→302 transient drop），\n      质疑 Cheetah 基线本身的不稳定性是否混淆了 CIVO 诊断。\n      Converged v/e 约 0.60-0.70，为 NVE normalization 提供基准。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah baseline cross-seed\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"eval_final\", \"eval_peak\", \"ve_ratio_converged\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"625\", \"625\", \"~0.65\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"520\", \"573\", \"~0.60\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"645\", \"645\", \"~0.65\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"597\", \"614\", \"~0.63\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah baseline 3-seed learning curves with IQM confidence band\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 确立但 inter-seed variance（CV≈11%）高于 Walker（CV≈3%），\n      这意味着 Cheetah 的 CIVO 检测需要更多 seeds 才能达到 Walker 的统计 power。\n      Median 档审稿人会指出此 asymmetry。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"Cheetah Run 中复制 CIVO trigger（dt=2 + subsample ON + trained dt_emb）\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 1\n      seed0_nve_peak: 70.64\n      seed0_civo: true\n      seed0_collapse_type: \"catastrophic\"\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 52\n      seed1_nve_peak: 8.27\n      seed1_civo: true\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 85\n      seed2_nve_peak: 12.5\n      seed2_civo: true\n      civo_rate: \"3/3 (100%)\"\n      mean_nve_peak: 30.5\n      cheetah_vs_walker_severity: \"Cheetah CIVO severity >> Walker (mean NVE 30x vs 3x)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah 已有 2 seeds 数据（s0: NVE=70.64 catastrophic, s1/exp_010b: NVE=8.27 severe）。\n      Cheetah 的 CIVO 比 Walker 严重得多——NVE 峰值 8-70x vs Walker 的 2-4x。\n      这是因为 Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 更大（更高维运动学 → dt>1 预测更难）。\n      预测 seed 2 也会 CIVO（NVE ~10-15x），给出 3/3 = 100% 崩溃率。\n      Median 档认为这强化了 C1/C2 的跨环境泛化，但会质疑：\n      (a) Cheetah 的 CIVO 动力学与 Walker 定性不同（更早、更严重），是否真是同一机制？\n      (b) 仅 2 个环境（Walker + Cheetah）不够 claim \"generalizes\"——3 环境是最低限度。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah CIVO trigger cross-seed\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"NVE peak\", \"Collapse type\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"~1\", \"70.64\", \"catastrophic\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"52\", \"8.27\", \"severe\"]\n          - [\"s2 (predicted)\", \"~85\", \"~12.5\", \"severe\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah NVE time series 3 seeds vs Walker 3 seeds, showing environment-dependent severity\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 的 100% 崩溃率（vs Walker 50%）和更高 NVE 峰值是双刃剑：\n      强化了 CIVO 是真实威胁，但也暗示 Walker 的 50% 可能是偏低的 — 环境越难 CIVO 越强。\n      Median 档审稿人接受跨环境 CIVO 存在性但认为 severity 差异（10x）需要解释：\n      是 RSSM capacity 差异还是 task complexity 差异？\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: \"Cheetah Run 因果控制：去掉 dt_embedding 是否阻止 CIVO\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 97\n      seed0_nve_peak: 0.20\n      seed0_civo: false\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 77\n      seed1_nve_peak: 0.10\n      seed1_civo: false\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 90\n      seed2_nve_peak: 0.15\n      seed2_civo: false\n      civo_prevention_rate: \"3/3 (100%)\"\n      mean_eval_vs_baseline: \"15%\"\n      reward_MAE_vs_baseline: \">50x\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有 2 seeds：s0 eval=96.5（NVE 0.2, no CIVO），s1 eval=77.3（NVE 0.1, no CIVO）。\n      与 Walker 008f 一致：去掉 dt_embedding 完全阻止 CIVO，但 eval 严重退化（仅 ~15% baseline）。\n      Cheetah 的退化比 Walker 更严重（Walker 008f 达 55% baseline），因为 Cheetah 对 reward prediction 更敏感。\n      Median 档接受因果控制成立（5/5 across 2 environments: no dt_emb → no CIVO），\n      但再次质疑：这是 \"prevention\" 还是 \"feature removal leading to functional impairment\"？\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-environment causal control (dt_embed_dim=0)\"\n        columns: [\"Environment\", \"Seeds\", \"CIVO rate\", \"Mean eval vs baseline\", \"Reward MAE ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"3 (s0, s3, s4)\", \"0/3\", \"~40%\", \"75x\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"2-3\", \"0/3\", \"~15%\", \">50x\"]\n          - [\"Combined\", \"5-6\", \"0/5+\", \"~30%\", \">>1x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: CIVO rate and eval retention for dt_embed_dim=0 across environments\"\n    analysis: >\n      因果控制在 Cheetah 中复现，5/5 完美分离确认 dt_embedding 是 CIVO 的必要条件。\n      但 eval 退化在 Cheetah 更严重，暴露了一个 tension：去掉 dt_embedding \"治愈\" CIVO\n      但也移除了 dt-conditioning 的功能价值。这对 \"CIVO 是 dt-conditioning 不可避免的副作用\" 的叙事有利，\n      但审稿人会要求解释为什么不能 have both（有效 conditioning + 无 CIVO）。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"Cheetah Run 中验证 unexposed trained dt_emb 的值抑制效果\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 532\n      seed0_nve_105K: 0.49\n      seed0_civo: false\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 504\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.48\n      seed1_civo: false\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 480\n      seed2_nve_105K: 0.52\n      seed2_civo: false\n      mean_eval_vs_baseline: \"85%\"\n      nve_range: \"0.48-0.52\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有 2 seeds：s0=532（NVE 0.49），s1=504（NVE 0.48）。Unexposed dt_emb 在 Cheetah 中也有效：\n      NVE < 1.0x，eval 保留 ~85% baseline。与 Walker 008a 一致（84% baseline）。\n      这是 C3 跨环境验证的最强数据：两个环境的 unexposed dt_emb 均表现出值抑制 + 高 eval 保留。\n      Median 档接受 C3 但认为 \"unexposed = subsample OFF\" 只是一种 workaround，\n      不是对 CIVO 机制的根本解决。\"如果你不让模型见到 dt>1 数据，当然不会 CIVO——但这也失去了 temporal abstraction 的目的。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"C3 cross-environment: unexposed dt_emb\"\n        columns: [\"Environment\", \"Seeds\", \"Mean eval vs baseline\", \"NVE range\", \"CIVO\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"3\", \"84%\", \"0.33-0.93\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"2-3\", \"85%\", \"0.48-0.52\", \"0/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-environment eval retention bar chart: unexposed dt_emb vs baseline vs trained dt_emb\"\n    analysis: >\n      C3 获得跨环境确认（6 seeds, 0 CIVO, 84-85% baseline），是论文中最 robust 的正面结果。\n      但 median 档正确指出这不是 mitigation——它避开了问题而非解决问题。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Diagnostic analyses (plans 030-034)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: \"量化不同模型在 dt=1 和 dt=2 上的 RSSM 预测质量差距\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_obs_gap: 2.04\n      baseline_reward_gap: 1.56\n      008d_obs_gap: 1.30\n      008d_reward_gap: 2.78\n      008f_obs_gap: 2.75\n      008f_reward_gap: 1.01\n      008d_dt1_obs_MSE: 41.31\n      baseline_dt1_obs_MSE: 13.49\n      key_finding: \"008d 的低 obs gap (1.30x) 具误导性——其 dt=1 绝对误差已是 baseline 3x\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      RSSM fidelity 分析已完成（exp_rssm_fidelity_analysis）。核心发现：\n      008d 的 obs gap ratio 看起来最小（1.30x），但绝对误差最大（dt1: 41.31 vs baseline 13.49），\n      说明模型整体已崩塌，gap ratio 失去意义。008f 的 reward gap (1.01x) 说明无 dt_embedding 时\n      reward head 无法区分 dt=1/dt=2——这是 \"功能丧失\" 不是 \"改善\"。\n      Median 档审稿人认为这是 \"expected and confirmatory\"——RSSM 在 dt>1 预测不好是已知的，\n      novelty 不在发现本身而在它与 CIVO 的因果连接。但审稿人会质疑：\n      只有 1 个 checkpoint 的分析，如何确认这是训练全程的 pattern 而非特定 step 的 artifact？\n    tables:\n      - name: \"RSSM Fidelity Table\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"dt1 obs_MSE\", \"dt2 obs_MSE\", \"obs gap\", \"dt1 reward_MAE\", \"dt2 reward_MAE\", \"reward gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"baseline\", \"13.49\", \"27.50\", \"2.04x\", \"0.0102\", \"0.0159\", \"1.56x\"]\n          - [\"008d (trained dt_emb)\", \"41.31\", \"53.67\", \"1.30x\", \"0.0568\", \"0.1579\", \"2.78x\"]\n          - [\"008f (no dt_emb)\", \"8.01\", \"22.04\", \"2.75x\", \"0.7469\", \"0.7526\", \"1.01x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart with both absolute values and ratios side-by-side, preventing ratio-only misleading\"\n    analysis: >\n      RSSM fidelity 分析确认了机制假说但未超越 \"supporting evidence\"。\n      Median 档给这个分析 moderate credit 但不视为独立贡献。\n      建议在 rebuttal 中加入训练过程中 fidelity 的演化曲线（多 checkpoint），回应 \"single snapshot\" 质疑。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: \"对比健康 vs 崩溃配置的 actor entropy 演化\"\n    expected_results:\n      healthy_008a_entropy_trend: \"稳定在 -4.5 to -5.2 范围\"\n      healthy_008c_entropy_trend: \"缓慢下降 -3.5 → -4.8\"\n      collapsed_006_entropy_trend: \"下降后回弹 -3.5 → -4.9 → -3.8\"\n      collapsed_008d_entropy_trend: \"持续下降 -1.9 → -4.9\"\n      collapsed_008e_v3_s2_entropy_trend: \"先降后升 -5.2 → -3.8 (反常)\"\n      pathway_A_signature: \"entropy ↓ (policy 过度确定化)\"\n      pathway_B_signature: \"entropy ↑ (policy destabilization)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Actor entropy 分析是区分 Pathway A (CIVO) 和 Pathway B (IRD) 的关键诊断工具。\n      经典 CIVO (008d): value overestimate → actor exploit → entropy 下降 → 策略变得过度确定。\n      非 CIVO 崩溃 (008e_v3_s2): eval 先跌 → value 滞后 → entropy 上升 → 策略变得随机。\n      Median 档认为这是 \"useful characterization\" 但不是 \"novel contribution\"——\n      entropy 作为策略健康度指标是标准做法，两种 pathway 的区分缺乏 formal framework。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Entropy trajectory comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Config\", \"Entropy@35K\", \"Entropy@55K\", \"Entropy@85K\", \"Entropy@105K\", \"Pathway\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"008a s0 (healthy)\", \"-4.2\", \"-4.5\", \"-4.8\", \"-5.0\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"008d s0 (CIVO)\", \"-3.5\", \"-4.9\", \"—\", \"—\", \"A\"]\n          - [\"008e_v3 s2 (IRD)\", \"-3.5\", \"-5.1\", \"-5.2\", \"-3.8\", \"B\"]\n          - [\"016e (SGS)\", \"-2.1\", \"-3.6\", \"-4.3\", \"—\", \"A (delayed)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Entropy vs step: healthy configs (blue band) vs CIVO (red, entropy ↓) vs IRD (orange, entropy ↑)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Entropy 分析确认两种崩溃 pathway 的存在，但 n=1-2 per pathway 不足以 formalize。\n      Median 档审稿人建议：如果要将 dual-pathway 作为贡献，需要至少 5 seeds per pathway 并做 statistical test。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: \"V(s) vs Monte Carlo return 分布对比\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_dt_emb_divergence: \"V(s) 分布右偏移 + 重尾，MC return 集中在低区间\"\n      untrained_dt_emb_match: \"V(s) 和 MC return 分布大致重叠，V(s) 略微左移\"\n      collapsed_state: \"V(s) 均值远超 MC return p95，完全脱钩\"\n      healthy_calibration: \"V(s) 中位数在 MC return IQR 内\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是对 v/e ratio proxy 的补充验证。直接展示 V(s) 分布 vs 实际回报分布比单一 ratio 更具信息量。\n      Median 档审稿人在 R3 中质疑 v/e ratio 是 crude proxy——这个分析直接回应。\n      预期结果：trained dt_emb 的 V(s) 明显偏高且扩散，untrained 的则接近校准。\n      但审稿人仍会指出：MC return 在 imagination 中不可直接计算（需要 ground truth environment），\n      只能用 eval return 作为 proxy，引入额外近似误差。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 violin plot panel: (trained/untrained) × (pre-collapse/post-collapse), V(s) distribution in orange vs MC return in blue\"\n    analysis: >\n      Distributional 分析增加了 R3 的防御深度，但实现依赖 eval return 作为 MC return proxy，\n      审稿人可能认为这只是换了一种方式展示同样的信息。Median 档给 minor positive credit。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: \"分析 dt=1 和 dt=2 embedding 向量的演化\"\n    expected_results:\n      initial_cosine_sim: \"~0.0 (random init)\"\n      trained_25K_cosine_sim: \"~0.3\"\n      trained_55K_cosine_sim: \"~0.65\"\n      trained_105K_cosine_sim: \"~0.75 (converging)\"\n      l2_distance_trend: \"monotonically increasing\"\n      frozen_cosine_sim: \"constant at ~0.0\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trained dt_embedding 的 dt=1 和 dt=2 向量会在训练过程中逐渐分离（cosine sim 从 ~0 增加，\n      但 L2 距离增加），说明 embedding 学到了 dt-specific representation。\n      Frozen embedding 保持初始状态不变（cosine sim ≈ 0）。\n      Median 档认为这是 \"descriptive visualization\"——确认 embedding 在训练，但不提供超越已知的 insight。\n      审稿人的反应：nice plot, but what does it tell us that we didn't already know from the gradient analysis?\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: cosine similarity between dt=1 and dt=2 embedding vectors over training steps, for trained vs frozen\"\n    analysis: >\n      Low priority（P2）合理。Cosine similarity 分析提供视觉直觉但不支撑任何独立 claim。\n      Median 档中这会出现在 appendix 如果提交，不会影响评分。\n\n  - name: \"NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_034\"\n    description: \"在不同阈值（1.3x, 1.5x, 1.7x, 2.0x）下计算分类准确率和 AUROC\"\n    expected_results:\n      threshold_1.3x_accuracy: 0.86\n      threshold_1.5x_accuracy: 0.93\n      threshold_1.7x_accuracy: 0.90\n      threshold_2.0x_accuracy: 0.83\n      youden_optimal_threshold: 1.53\n      AUROC_walker: 0.98\n      AUROC_cheetah: 0.95\n      AUROC_combined: 0.969\n      AUROC_bootstrap_95CI: \"[0.91, 1.00]\"\n      n_total_datapoints: 29\n      leave_one_env_out_AUROC_walker_train: 0.97\n      leave_one_env_out_AUROC_cheetah_test: 0.92\n    result_rationale: >\n      NVE 阈值分析基于所有可用 seeds（~29 数据点跨 4 环境）。1.5x 是 near-optimal（Youden index 收敛到 1.53x），\n      AUROC 0.969 表明 NVE 是 strong discriminator。\n      但 median 档审稿人一致标记（Dream D8）：阈值在同数据集上 calibrate 和 validate = in-sample bias。\n      Leave-one-environment-out CV 部分回应这个问题（Cheetah 作为 held-out 时 AUROC 仍 ~0.92），\n      但只有 2 个环境做 LOO-CV 统计意义有限。\n      Bootstrap 95% CI [0.91, 1.00] 看起来 impressive 但样本量小时 bootstrap CI 本身偏乐观。\n      这是 median 档的核心方法论弱点之一。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"NVE threshold ROC analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Threshold\", \"Sensitivity\", \"Specificity\", \"Accuracy\", \"Youden J\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"1.3x\", \"0.94\", \"0.80\", \"0.86\", \"0.74\"]\n          - [\"1.5x\", \"0.88\", \"1.00\", \"0.93\", \"0.88\"]\n          - [\"1.53x (optimal)\", \"0.88\", \"1.00\", \"0.93\", \"0.88\"]\n          - [\"1.7x\", \"0.81\", \"1.00\", \"0.90\", \"0.81\"]\n          - [\"2.0x\", \"0.69\", \"1.00\", \"0.83\", \"0.69\"]\n      - name: \"Leave-one-environment-out AUROC\"\n        columns: [\"Train env\", \"Test env\", \"AUROC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker\", \"Cheetah\", \"0.92\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"Walker\", \"0.97\"]\n          - [\"Combined\", \"Combined (bootstrap)\", \"0.969 [0.91, 1.00]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ROC curve with 95% bootstrap CI band, marking Youden-optimal threshold\"\n    analysis: >\n      AUROC 0.969 是 C2 的最强定量结果，但 in-sample calibration 和 n=29 是不可回避的限制。\n      Median 档审稿人接受 NVE 作为 diagnostic tool 但不接受 1.5x 作为 generalizable threshold。\n      Rebuttal 策略：承认 limitation，强调 leave-one-env-out 结果（虽然 n 小但方向正确），\n      将 NVE threshold generalization 定位为 future work。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Cartpole Swingup (plans 050-052) — third environment\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_050\"\n    description: \"第三个 DMC 环境的 dt=1 baseline，扩展到非 locomotion 任务\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_500K: 860\n      seed1_eval_return_500K: 845\n      seed2_eval_return_500K: 870\n      cross_seed_mean: 858\n      cross_seed_std: 13\n      ve_ratio_converged: \"0.65-0.75\"\n      convergence_step: \"80K-120K\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole Swingup 是 DMC 中相对简单的任务，DreamerV3 baseline 应快速收敛到 ~850-870。\n      Inter-seed variance 预计低于 Cheetah（simpler dynamics → more consistent learning）。\n      v/e ratio 收敛到 0.65-0.75，与 Walker/Cheetah 一致。\n      Median 档审稿人认为加入第三个环境是正面的（从 \"minimum viable\" 的 3 环境升级），\n      但 Cartpole 作为相对简单任务可能不够挑战性——\"如果 CIVO 在简单任务上弱或不出现，\n      这削弱了 generalization claim 而非加强。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole baseline\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"eval@500K\", \"ve_ratio_converged\", \"convergence_step\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"860\", \"0.70\", \"100K\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"845\", \"0.68\", \"110K\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"870\", \"0.72\", \"90K\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole baseline learning curves, 3 seeds with confidence band\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 稳定。关键问题是 CIVO 在 Cartpole 的表现——如果弱于 Walker/Cheetah，\n      会被解读为 \"CIVO severity is task-dependent\"（median 档认可的弱化叙事）。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_051\"\n    description: \"Cartpole Swingup 中复制 CIVO trigger\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 520\n      seed0_nve_peak: 2.8\n      seed0_civo: true\n      seed0_collapse_type: \"partial — degradation without catastrophic collapse\"\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 680\n      seed1_nve_peak: 1.8\n      seed1_civo: true\n      seed1_collapse_type: \"mild — NVE borderline, eval recovers\"\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 350\n      seed2_nve_peak: 4.1\n      seed2_civo: true\n      seed2_collapse_type: \"moderate — sustained degradation\"\n      civo_rate: \"3/3 (NVE > 1.5x)\"\n      catastrophic_collapse_rate: \"0/3 (no complete collapse to random policy)\"\n      mean_eval_vs_baseline: \"60%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole 比 Cheetah 简单但比 Walker 的 observation space 更低维（5 vs 24 dim），\n      RSSM 在 dt>1 的预测误差相对较小。预期 CIVO 出现（NVE > 1.5x）但严重程度低于 Walker/Cheetah：\n      degradation 而非 catastrophic collapse。这是因为 Cartpole 的值函数 landscape 更平滑，\n      value overestimation 更容易被 self-correction 机制缓解。\n      Median 档审稿人会抓住这一点：\"CIVO severity 与任务复杂度相关——在简单任务上是 nuisance，\n      在复杂任务上才是 fatal。这限制了 diagnostic 的实际影响力。\"\n      但也会认可：CIVO 在所有 3 个环境中都出现（NVE > 1.5x），direction 一致。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-environment CIVO severity\"\n        columns: [\"Environment\", \"CIVO rate\", \"Mean NVE peak\", \"Catastrophic collapse rate\", \"Mean eval retention\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"2/4 (50%)\", \"2.7\", \"2/4\", \"47%\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"3/3 (100%)\", \"30.5\", \"2/3\", \"5%\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"3/3 (100%)\", \"2.9\", \"0/3\", \"60%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-environment CIVO heatmap: environment × seed, colored by NVE peak\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole 确认 CIVO 的 universality 但暴露了 severity 的强环境依赖性。\n      Median 档审稿人将此解读为 \"the phenomenon is real but its practical impact is task-dependent\"，\n      进一步将 novelty 定位为 incremental observation 而非 general finding。\n      NVE 阈值 1.5x 在 Cartpole 中仍有效（3/3 detection），增强了跨环境泛化的证据。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_052\"\n    description: \"Cartpole Swingup 因果控制（无 dt_embedding）\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 650\n      seed0_nve_peak: 0.35\n      seed0_civo: false\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 620\n      seed1_nve_peak: 0.40\n      seed1_civo: false\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 660\n      seed2_nve_peak: 0.30\n      seed2_civo: false\n      civo_prevention_rate: \"3/3 (100%)\"\n      mean_eval_vs_baseline: \"75%\"\n      reward_MAE_vs_baseline: \"~30x\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      无 dt_embedding 应阻止 CIVO（与 Walker/Cheetah 一致）。Cartpole 的 eval 保留（75%）\n      介于 Walker（40-55%）和 baseline 之间，因为 Cartpole 的 reward 结构更简单，\n      reward prediction 退化的影响相对较小。\n      Median 档审稿人：因果控制在第三个环境确认，累计 8/8 across 3 environments（no dt_emb → no CIVO）。\n      这是论文中最 robust 的因果结论之一。\n      但评论：\"因果控制只证明 dt_embedding 是 necessary condition，没有提供 mitigation pathway。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-environment causal control summary (final)\"\n        columns: [\"Environment\", \"Seeds\", \"CIVO prevented\", \"Eval retention\", \"Reward degradation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"3\", \"3/3\", \"40-55%\", \"75x MAE\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"2-3\", \"2-3/2-3\", \"~15%\", \">50x MAE\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"3\", \"3/3\", \"~75%\", \"~30x MAE\"]\n          - [\"**Total**\", \"**8-9**\", \"**8-9/8-9**\", \"**varies**\", \"**>>1x**\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar chart: eval retention by environment for dt_embed_dim=0\"\n    analysis: >\n      8/8+ 因果控制是 C2 的最终定量支撑。但 eval retention 的环境依赖性（15%-75%）\n      意味着 \"removing dt_embedding\" 的代价不一致，进一步说明 CIVO 问题没有 one-size-fits-all solution。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Advanced interventions (plan_060)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot (Walker Walk, 1 seed)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_060\"\n    description: \"监控 imagination rollout 中的 RSSM 预测不确定性，超过阈值时截断\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_return_105K: 380\n      nve_peak: 1.8\n      civo_delayed: true\n      civo_prevented: false\n      truncation_rate_avg: \"40% of rollout steps truncated\"\n      effective_horizon: \"H_eff ≈ 9 (from H=15)\"\n      eval_vs_baseline: \"41%\"\n      eval_vs_008d: \"2.7x better than 008d collapse\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Uncertainty-gated truncation 在概念上是对的（截断不确定预测避免 error compounding），\n      但在 DreamerV3 的 RSSM 中面临两个问题：\n      (1) RSSM 的 posterior entropy 不是 calibrated 的 uncertainty estimate——\n      高 entropy 可能反映 genuine uncertainty 也可能反映 poor representation；\n      (2) 截断降低了 effective horizon，相当于变相回到 H=8 的配置（已知性能较差）。\n      预测结果：CIVO 延迟但不完全阻止（NVE 仍达 1.8x），eval 中等（380 ≈ 41% baseline）。\n      Median 档审稿人：interesting pilot 但 1 seed 不足以 draw conclusions。\n      This could strengthen the intervention hierarchy as a 4th level (model-level gating)\n      but needs more work to be publishable.\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Intervention hierarchy with uncertainty gating\"\n        columns: [\"Level\", \"Method\", \"Success rate\", \"Mechanism\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"L1: Gradient\", \"SGS variants\", \"1/17\", \"Backward-pass insufficient\"]\n          - [\"L2: Output\", \"RAVE\", \"0/2\", \"EMA anchor polluted\"]\n          - [\"L3: Representation\", \"TCN\", \"2/8\", \"Narrow dose window\"]\n          - [\"L4: Model (new)\", \"Uncertainty truncation\", \"0/1 (pilot)\", \"Effective horizon reduction\"]\n          - [\"Control\", \"dt_emb removal\", \"8/8+\", \"Feature removal\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Truncation rate over training steps, overlaid with NVE and eval curves\"\n    analysis: >\n      Pilot 结果不够强支撑独立 claim，但为 intervention hierarchy 添加第四层。\n      Median 档中这会被定位为 \"preliminary evidence\" 放在 Discussion 中。\n      审稿人评价：interesting direction，please extend in camera-ready。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Hopper Hop (plan_040) — stretch goal\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: \"第三个 locomotion DMC 环境，3 configs (baseline, CIVO trigger, causal control) × 3 seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_mean_200K: 280\n      baseline_std: 45\n      civo_trigger_civo_rate: \"2/3\"\n      civo_trigger_mean_nve_peak: 5.2\n      civo_trigger_mean_eval_vs_baseline: \"25%\"\n      causal_control_civo_rate: \"0/3\"\n      causal_control_mean_eval_vs_baseline: \"35%\"\n      total_gpu_hours: 45\n    result_rationale: >\n      Hopper Hop 是比 Walker Walk 更难的 locomotion 任务（DreamerV3 baseline ~250-300）。\n      CIVO 预计出现但环境本身的 high variance 和 lower baseline 使 NVE normalization 更嘈杂。\n      2/3 崩溃率（比 Cheetah 的 3/3 低）因为 Hopper 的 value landscape 有不同 topology。\n      Median 档审稿人：第四个环境加强了 generalization 但仍是 DMC proprioceptive setting——\n      \"all four environments are DMC proprioceptive, how do we know this isn't a DMC-specific artifact?\"\n      Pixel observation 的缺失仍是 core weakness (Dream D9)。\n      45 GPU hours 的预算对 P2 priority 可能不被分配——median 档假设这个实验可能不做。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Four-environment CIVO summary\"\n        columns: [\"Environment\", \"Obs dim\", \"Baseline\", \"CIVO rate\", \"Causal control rate\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"24\", \"~950\", \"2/4 (50%)\", \"0/8 (0%)\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"17\", \"~600\", \"3/3 (100%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"5\", \"~860\", \"3/3 (100%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\"]\n          - [\"Hopper Hop\", \"15\", \"~280\", \"2/3 (67%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\"]\n          - [\"**Total**\", \"—\", \"—\", \"**10/13 (77%)**\", \"**0/17 (0%)**\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-environment radar chart: CIVO rate, severity, eval retention, causal control effectiveness\"\n    analysis: >\n      Hopper 的加入使总 CIVO detection 达 10/13（77%）和因果控制 0/17（100% prevention）。\n      但 median 档审稿人的核心攻击不在环境数量而在环境多样性：\n      全部 4 个都是 DMC continuous control + proprioceptive observation + RSSM。\n      要 \"truly generalize\" 需要不同 world model（IRIS/TWM）或 pixel observation。\n      此实验在 median 档中被视为 \"nice to have\" 而非 \"changes the verdict\"。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3e378428-3718-4c03-8413-20c57e8b82cc","total_cost_usd":1.2212569999999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14270,"cache_read_input_tokens":374006,"output_tokens":21300,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14270,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":16759,"cache_read_input_tokens":82591,"cache_creation_input_tokens":764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":764},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":52189,"outputTokens":22,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.052299,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":6,"outputTokens":21300,"cacheReadInputTokens":374006,"cacheCreationInputTokens":71908,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.168958,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"66de7ba3-d18e-4c39-8262-a1ab255c36c8"}
